@startuml SALUD_Pay_Module_78_pay_settlement
title Module 78 — pay-settlement: Cortes, payouts, cobros y conciliación\n(schema: pay_settlement)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide circle

' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' PERFIL PAY (D-18). Una base de PostgreSQL POR SERVICIO: este módulo describe la base `pay_settlement`,
' no un schema de la base de SALUD. Se genera con salud-db/gen_ddl_pay.py a SQL/pay/78_pay_settlement/ (objetos sin
' calificar: se crean en el esquema de la conexión). Portado el 2026-10-27 del DDL de referencia de
' services/pay-settlement/sql/ (pasarelapago). A partir de acá la fuente de verdad es ESTE archivo.
' SQL de referencia de pay-settlement (P2.H2.M1). A mover a mantra-core-health-model (D-18): el modelo todavía no existe.
' pay-settlement NUNCA guarda saldos (los saldos son del ledger): guarda el estado de sus procesos —cortes, payouts, cobros pendientes,
' corridas de conciliación y excepciones— y las marcas que le permiten repetir cualquier paso sin duplicar efectos.
' Montos en centavos de BOB (bigint). Las tablas técnicas outbox_events / inbox_events / idempotency_keys vienen de contracts/packages.
' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note as BIZ_diagram_78_pay_settlement
  BUSINESS PURPOSE
  Base propia del microservicio pay-settlement de la pasarela de pagos ALOVIDA (cortes, payouts, cobros y conciliación).
  Separación (regla #1 del plan maestro): ningún otro servicio lee estas tablas; los datos de otros
  servicios llegan por eventos o por sus APIs. Dinero en unidades menores enteras (amount_minor, BOB).
end note

' Modo (D-28): `test` o `live`, el de la CLAVE que hizo la petición (cabecera X-Pay-Mode). Todo registro que mueve o lee dinero lo lleva, toda consulta lo
' filtra, y se propaga al ledger y a los conectores. Un registro de un modo no se ve, no se cobra y no se paga desde el otro.
' Comercios que el servicio conoce (los que aparecieron en el ledger). Es un directorio SIN modo: los eventos `ledger.*` todavía no llevan `mode`
' (el AsyncAPI no lo declara), así que no se puede saber en qué modo vendió. Un comercio sin movimiento en un modo libera 0 en ese modo.
entity settlement_merchants {
  * merchant_id : text <<PK>>
  * first_seen_at : timestamptz
  * last_activity_at : timestamptz
}

' Marcas del corte por (modo, comercio). `watermark_at` y `residual_minor` hacen incremental el corte: lo cobrado antes de `watermark_at` ya se
' liberó, y `residual_minor` arrastra lo que quedó sin liberar (positivo) o lo que se devolvió de más (negativo) para que la ventana siguiente no lea
' el ledger desde el principio de los tiempos. Cada modo tiene su propio saldo en el ledger, así que cada uno lleva sus propias marcas.
entity settlement_merchant_marks {
  * mode : text <<PK>>
  * merchant_id : text <<PK, FK>>
    watermark_at : timestamptz
  * residual_minor : bigint
}

' Última versión del tarifario con abono mensual (evento fee_schedule.published). Una versión vieja nunca pisa a una nueva.
entity settlement_fee_plans {
  * merchant_id : text <<PK>>
  * version : integer
  * monthly_fee_minor : bigint
  * effective_from : timestamptz
    effective_to : timestamptz
  * updated_at : timestamptz
}

' Un lote por modo y fecha de corte: `(mode, cutoff_date)` única es la idempotencia del corte (REQ-P2-5).
entity settlement_batches {
  ' sb_<base>
  * id : text <<PK>>
  * mode : text
  * cutoff_date : date
  * release_days : integer
  * release_before : timestamptz
  * period_from : timestamptz
  * status : text
  * merchants_count : integer
  * released_minor : bigint
  * payouts_count : integer
  * failed_count : integer
  * created_at : timestamptz
    completed_at : timestamptz
}

' Un renglón por comercio y lote: lo planeado se guarda ANTES de tocar el ledger, así un reintento repite exactamente lo mismo.
entity settlement_batch_items {
  * batch_id : text <<PK, FK>>
  * merchant_id : text <<PK>>
  * status : text
    window_from : timestamptz
    planned_release_minor : bigint
    new_residual_minor : bigint
  * ledger_attempt : integer
    release_ref : text
  * released_minor : bigint
  ' Deuda del comercio en `merchant:{id}:debt` (lo que un contracargo perdido dejó por encima de su saldo pendiente, D-22) que el corte netea moviendo disponible → deuda.
  ' NULL = todavía no planeado; el monto se fija ANTES de llamar al ledger, como el de la liberación.
    netting_minor : bigint
  * netting_attempt : integer
    payout_id : text
    failure_code : text
  * updated_at : timestamptz
}

' Pagos a comercios. `step` es el avance interno de la máquina (created → held → sent → resolved); `status` es el público.
entity settlement_payouts {
  ' po_<base>
  * id : text <<PK>>
  * mode : text
  * merchant_id : text
  * amount_minor : bigint
  * currency : char(3)
  * rail : text
  * simulated : boolean
  * reason : text
  * status : text
  * step : text
    hold_id : text
  * hold_business_ref : text
    rail_reference : text
    batch_id : text <<FK>>
  * requested_by : text
    failure_code : text
  * period_from : timestamptz
  * period_to : timestamptz
  * created_at : timestamptz
  * updated_at : timestamptz
    paid_at : timestamptz
}

' Cobros a un comercio que se netean contra su saldo: abono mensual (D-07), comisión programada de proveedores (7.8) y deuda por
' contracargo (D-22). Una vez por (comercio, tipo, periodo): ese es el «una sola vez por mes» de P2.H2.M9.
entity settlement_charges {
  ' cg_<base>
  * id : text <<PK>>
  * mode : text
  * merchant_id : text
  * kind : text
  ' 2026-11 para el abono; la referencia del llamador en los demás
  * period_key : text
  ' platform:fees (abono, comisión) o connector:<x>:clearing (contracargo)
  * credit_account : text
  * ledger_code : text
  * amount_minor : bigint
  * collected_minor : bigint
  * status : text
  * requested_by : text
  * created_at : timestamptz
    collected_at : timestamptz
}

' Cada intento de cobro contra el saldo. El monto se fija antes de llamar al ledger y su referencia es única por (cobro, seq).
entity settlement_charge_collections {
  * charge_id : text <<PK, FK>>
  * seq : integer <<PK>>
  * amount_minor : bigint
  * ledger_ref : text
  * status : text
  * created_at : timestamptz
}

' Corridas de conciliación.
entity settlement_reconciliation_runs {
  ' rr_<base>
  * id : text <<PK>>
  * mode : text
  * connector : text
  * period_from : timestamptz
  * period_to : timestamptz
  * source : text
  * status : text
  * matched_count : integer
  * exception_count : integer
  * ignored_count : integer
    failure_code : text
  * requested_by : text
  * created_at : timestamptz
    completed_at : timestamptz
}

' Las líneas del extracto que se leyeron. Se descarta la glosa del banco (puede traer datos personales).
entity settlement_statement_lines {
  * run_id : text <<PK, FK>>
  ' extracto#n: referencia opaca, nunca el texto de la línea
  * line_ref : text <<PK>>
  * provider_reference : text
    our_reference : text
  * direction : text
  * amount_minor : bigint
  * value_date : date
    booked_at : timestamptz
  * outcome : text
}

' Diferencias que una persona tiene que mirar. El ledger NO se ajusta solo (REQ-P2-6). `dedupe_key` evita reabrir la misma
' diferencia en cada corrida.
' `payment_contradiction` NO sale de una corrida: la abre el consumidor de `payment_intent.contradiction_detected` (pay-payments), por eso
' no tiene corrida ni conector (`run_id` y `connector` NULL), y `mode` puede ser NULL si el productor no lo informó (visible desde los dos
' modos hasta que una persona la resuelva). Las demás exigen corrida, conector y modo.
entity settlement_exceptions {
  ' rx_<base>
  * id : text <<PK>>
    mode : text
    run_id : text <<FK>>
    connector : text
  * kind : text
    provider_reference : text
    business_ref : text
    statement_amount_minor : bigint
    ledger_amount_minor : bigint
  * difference_minor : bigint
  * statement_line_ref : text
    merchant_id : text
    payment_intent_id : text
  ' solo payment_contradiction: {kind, current_status, incoming_status, detected_at}; sin datos personales
    source_detail : jsonb
  * status : text
    resolution : text
    resolved_by : text
    resolution_note : text
    resolved_at : timestamptz
  * dedupe_key : char(64)
  * created_at : timestamptz
}

' Un pedido de ajuste NO mueve dinero: lo toma el flujo normal de asientos con su propia aprobación.
entity settlement_adjustment_requests {
  * id : bigint <<PK>>
  * exception_id : text <<FK>>
  * requested_by : text
  * difference_minor : bigint
  * note : text
  * status : text
  * created_at : timestamptz
}

' Auditoría de las decisiones de personas (quién decidió, con qué rol, sobre qué). Solo se agrega.
entity settlement_audit {
  * id : bigint <<PK>>
  * actor : text
  * role : text
  * action : text
  * subject : text
  * detail : jsonb
  * at : timestamptz
}

' Tablas técnicas de @pay/outbox. Cada servicio las tiene en SU base. Se declaran en el modelo (D-18).
' Tabla técnica de @pay/outbox: la declara la librería y cada servicio la tiene en SU base.
entity outbox_events {
  ' id del CloudEvent; también es el Nats-Msg-Id
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  ' orden de publicación
  * seq : bigserial
  * aggregate_type : text
  * aggregate_id : text
  * type : text
  ' tema NATS destino
  * subject : text
  ' el CloudEvent completo
  * envelope : jsonb
  * created_at : timestamptz
    published_at : timestamptz
  * attempts : integer
    last_error : text
}

' Tabla técnica de @pay/outbox: la declara la librería y cada servicio la tiene en SU base.
entity inbox_events {
  ' qué consumidor procesó el evento
  * consumer : text <<PK>>
  * event_id : text <<PK>>
  * processed_at : timestamptz
}

' Tabla técnica de @pay/idempotency. Cada servicio la tiene en SU base (regla de separación #1).
' Se declara en el modelo (mantra-core-health-model, D-18) y se aplica por el pipeline; este archivo es la referencia.
' Tabla técnica de @pay/idempotency: la declara la librería y cada servicio la tiene en SU base.
entity idempotency_keys {
  ' quién: el id del comercio
  * scope : text <<PK>>
  ' la Idempotency-Key del cliente
  * key : text <<PK>>
  ' sha256 de método + ruta + cuerpo canónico
  * request_hash : text
  * state : text
  ' hasta dónde llegó la ejecución
  * recovery_point : text
    response_status : integer
    response_body : jsonb
  ' null = nadie la está ejecutando
    locked_at : timestamptz
  ' identifica a quien la ejecuta (compare-and-set)
    lock_token : text
  * created_at : timestamptz
  * expires_at : timestamptz
}

settlement_merchant_marks }o--|| settlement_merchants : merchant_id
settlement_batch_items }o--|| settlement_batches : batch_id
settlement_payouts }o--|| settlement_batches : batch_id
settlement_charge_collections }o--|| settlement_charges : charge_id
settlement_statement_lines }o--|| settlement_reconciliation_runs : run_id
settlement_exceptions }o--|| settlement_reconciliation_runs : run_id
settlement_adjustment_requests }o--|| settlement_exceptions : exception_id

entity "INDEXES · settlement_merchants" as idxset_settlement_merchants <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_merchants : (merchant_id) UNIQUE BTREE
}
settlement_merchants .. idxset_settlement_merchants : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_merchant_marks" as idxset_settlement_merchant_marks <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_merchant_marks : (mode, merchant_id) UNIQUE BTREE
}
settlement_merchant_marks .. idxset_settlement_merchant_marks : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_fee_plans" as idxset_settlement_fee_plans <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_fee_plans : (merchant_id) UNIQUE BTREE
}
settlement_fee_plans .. idxset_settlement_fee_plans : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_batches" as idxset_settlement_batches <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_batches : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK settlement_batches_cutoff_unique : (mode, cutoff_date) UNIQUE BTREE
}
settlement_batches .. idxset_settlement_batches : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_batch_items" as idxset_settlement_batch_items <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_batch_items : (batch_id, merchant_id) UNIQUE BTREE
}
settlement_batch_items .. idxset_settlement_batch_items : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_payouts" as idxset_settlement_payouts <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_payouts : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK settlement_payouts_batch_merchant_unique : (batch_id, merchant_id) UNIQUE BTREE WHERE batch_id IS NOT NULL
  IX settlement_payouts_merchant_page : (mode, merchant_id, created_at DESC, id DESC) BTREE
  IX settlement_payouts_open : (updated_at) BTREE WHERE step <> 'resolved'
}
settlement_payouts .. idxset_settlement_payouts : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_charges" as idxset_settlement_charges <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_charges : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK settlement_charges_period_unique : (mode, merchant_id, kind, period_key) UNIQUE BTREE
  IX settlement_charges_open : (mode, merchant_id) BTREE WHERE status = 'open'
}
settlement_charges .. idxset_settlement_charges : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_charge_collections" as idxset_settlement_charge_collections <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_charge_collections : (charge_id, seq) UNIQUE BTREE
}
settlement_charge_collections .. idxset_settlement_charge_collections : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_reconciliation_runs" as idxset_settlement_reconciliation_runs <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_reconciliation_runs : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
}
settlement_reconciliation_runs .. idxset_settlement_reconciliation_runs : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_statement_lines" as idxset_settlement_statement_lines <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_statement_lines : (run_id, line_ref) UNIQUE BTREE
}
settlement_statement_lines .. idxset_settlement_statement_lines : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_exceptions" as idxset_settlement_exceptions <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_exceptions : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK settlement_exceptions_dedupe_unique : (dedupe_key) UNIQUE BTREE
  IX settlement_exceptions_page : (mode, created_at DESC, id DESC) BTREE
  IX settlement_exceptions_run : (run_id) BTREE
}
settlement_exceptions .. idxset_settlement_exceptions : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_adjustment_requests" as idxset_settlement_adjustment_requests <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_adjustment_requests : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK settlement_adjustment_requests_exception_unique : (exception_id) UNIQUE BTREE
}
settlement_adjustment_requests .. idxset_settlement_adjustment_requests : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · settlement_audit" as idxset_settlement_audit <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_settlement_audit : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
}
settlement_audit .. idxset_settlement_audit : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · outbox_events" as idxset_outbox_events <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_outbox_events : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK outbox_events_seq_key : (seq) UNIQUE BTREE
  IX outbox_events_pending_idx : (seq) BTREE WHERE published_at IS NULL
}
outbox_events .. idxset_outbox_events : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · inbox_events" as idxset_inbox_events <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_inbox_events : (consumer, event_id) UNIQUE BTREE
}
inbox_events .. idxset_inbox_events : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · idempotency_keys" as idxset_idempotency_keys <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_idempotency_keys : (scope, key) UNIQUE BTREE
  IX idempotency_keys_expires_at_idx : (expires_at) BTREE
}
idempotency_keys .. idxset_idempotency_keys : indexed by

entity "PAY EXTRAS · pay_settlement" as pay_extras_pay_settlement <<PAY_EXTRAS>> {
  ' Lo que el generador base (gen_ddl.py) no expresa: defaults no booleanos, identidades, CHECK, FK compuestas,
  ' funciones, triggers y datos semilla. Lo materializa salud-db/gen_ddl_pay.py (05_constraints.sql / 06_seed.sql).
  DEFAULT settlement_merchants.first_seen_at : now()
  DEFAULT settlement_merchants.last_activity_at : now()
  DEFAULT settlement_merchant_marks.residual_minor : 0
  CHECK_SQL settlement_merchant_marks : settlement_merchant_marks_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  DEFAULT settlement_fee_plans.monthly_fee_minor : 0
  DEFAULT settlement_fee_plans.updated_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL settlement_fee_plans : settlement_fee_plans_version_check | version >= 1
  CHECK_SQL settlement_fee_plans : settlement_fee_plans_monthly_fee_minor_check | monthly_fee_minor >= 0
  DEFAULT settlement_batches.merchants_count : 0
  DEFAULT settlement_batches.released_minor : 0
  DEFAULT settlement_batches.payouts_count : 0
  DEFAULT settlement_batches.failed_count : 0
  DEFAULT settlement_batches.created_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL settlement_batches : settlement_batches_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_batches : settlement_batches_release_days_check | release_days BETWEEN 0 AND 60
  CHECK_SQL settlement_batches : settlement_batches_status_check | status IN ('running', 'completed', 'failed')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_batches : settlement_batches_released_minor_check | released_minor >= 0
  DEFAULT settlement_batch_items.ledger_attempt : 1
  DEFAULT settlement_batch_items.released_minor : 0
  DEFAULT settlement_batch_items.netting_attempt : 1
  DEFAULT settlement_batch_items.updated_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL settlement_batch_items : settlement_batch_items_status_check | status IN ('pending', 'planned', 'released', 'done', 'failed')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_batch_items : settlement_batch_items_planned_release_minor_check | planned_release_minor >= 0
  CHECK_SQL settlement_batch_items : settlement_batch_items_ledger_attempt_check | ledger_attempt >= 1
  CHECK_SQL settlement_batch_items : settlement_batch_items_released_minor_check | released_minor >= 0
  CHECK_SQL settlement_batch_items : settlement_batch_items_netting_minor_check | netting_minor >= 0
  CHECK_SQL settlement_batch_items : settlement_batch_items_netting_attempt_check | netting_attempt >= 1
  DEFAULT settlement_payouts.created_at : now()
  DEFAULT settlement_payouts.updated_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL settlement_payouts : settlement_payouts_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_payouts : settlement_payouts_amount_minor_check | amount_minor >= 1
  CHECK_SQL settlement_payouts : settlement_payouts_rail_check | rail IN ('bank_transfer', 'acquirer_settlement')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_payouts : settlement_payouts_reason_check | reason IN ('weekly_cut', 'mandate_obligation', 'mandate_commission', 'manual')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_payouts : settlement_payouts_status_check | status IN ('pending', 'in_transit', 'paid', 'failed')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_payouts : settlement_payouts_step_check | step IN ('created', 'held', 'sent', 'resolved')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_payouts : settlement_payouts_terminal_consistency | (status IN ('paid', 'failed')) = (step = 'resolved')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_payouts : settlement_payouts_failure_consistency | (status = 'failed') = (failure_code IS NOT NULL)
  DEFAULT settlement_charges.collected_minor : 0
  DEFAULT settlement_charges.created_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL settlement_charges : settlement_charges_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_charges : settlement_charges_kind_check | kind IN ('monthly_fee', 'provider_commission', 'chargeback_debt')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_charges : settlement_charges_ledger_code_check | ledger_code IN ('fee', 'refund')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_charges : settlement_charges_amount_minor_check | amount_minor >= 1
  CHECK_SQL settlement_charges : settlement_charges_check | collected_minor >= 0 AND collected_minor <= amount_minor
  CHECK_SQL settlement_charges : settlement_charges_status_check | status IN ('open', 'collected')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_charges : settlement_charges_status_consistency | (status = 'collected') = (collected_minor = amount_minor)
  DEFAULT settlement_charge_collections.created_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL settlement_charge_collections : settlement_charge_collections_seq_check | seq >= 1
  CHECK_SQL settlement_charge_collections : settlement_charge_collections_amount_minor_check | amount_minor >= 1
  CHECK_SQL settlement_charge_collections : settlement_charge_collections_status_check | status IN ('planned', 'posted', 'rejected')
  DEFAULT settlement_reconciliation_runs.matched_count : 0
  DEFAULT settlement_reconciliation_runs.exception_count : 0
  DEFAULT settlement_reconciliation_runs.ignored_count : 0
  DEFAULT settlement_reconciliation_runs.created_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL settlement_reconciliation_runs : settlement_reconciliation_runs_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_reconciliation_runs : settlement_reconciliation_runs_source_check | source IN ('api', 'csv', 'camt053')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_reconciliation_runs : settlement_reconciliation_runs_status_check | status IN ('running', 'completed', 'failed')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_statement_lines : settlement_statement_lines_direction_check | direction IN ('credit', 'debit')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_statement_lines : settlement_statement_lines_amount_minor_check | amount_minor >= 0
  CHECK_SQL settlement_statement_lines : settlement_statement_lines_outcome_check | outcome IN ('matched', 'exception', 'ignored')
  DEFAULT settlement_exceptions.created_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL settlement_exceptions : settlement_exceptions_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_exceptions : settlement_exceptions_kind_check | kind IN ('missing_in_ledger', 'missing_in_statement', 'amount_mismatch', 'duplicate_in_statement', 'unknown_reference', 'payment_contradiction')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_exceptions : settlement_exceptions_statement_amount_minor_check | statement_amount_minor >= 0
  CHECK_SQL settlement_exceptions : settlement_exceptions_ledger_amount_minor_check | ledger_amount_minor >= 0
  CHECK_SQL settlement_exceptions : settlement_exceptions_status_check | status IN ('open', 'resolved', 'dismissed')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_exceptions : settlement_exceptions_resolution_check | resolution IN ('request_adjustment', 'dismiss')
  CHECK_SQL settlement_exceptions : settlement_exceptions_resolution_note_check | char_length(resolution_note) <= 500
  CHECK_SQL settlement_exceptions : settlement_exceptions_origin_shape | (kind = 'payment_contradiction' AND run_id IS NULL AND connector IS NULL AND source_detail IS NOT NULL) OR (kind <> 'payment_contradiction' AND run_id IS NOT NULL AND connector IS NOT NULL AND mode IS NOT NULL AND source_detail IS NULL)
  CHECK_SQL settlement_exceptions : settlement_exceptions_resolution_consistency | (status = 'open') = (resolution IS NULL)
  IDENTITY settlement_adjustment_requests.id
  DEFAULT settlement_adjustment_requests.status : 'requested'
  DEFAULT settlement_adjustment_requests.created_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL settlement_adjustment_requests : settlement_adjustment_requests_status_check | status IN ('requested')
  IDENTITY settlement_audit.id
  DEFAULT settlement_audit.detail : '{}'::jsonb
  DEFAULT settlement_audit.at : now()
  DEFAULT outbox_events.created_at : now()
  DEFAULT outbox_events.attempts : 0
  DEFAULT inbox_events.processed_at : now()
  DEFAULT idempotency_keys.recovery_point : 'started'
  DEFAULT idempotency_keys.created_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL idempotency_keys : idempotency_keys_state_check | state IN ('started', 'completed')
  FUNCTION forbid_mutation
  | CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION forbid_mutation() RETURNS trigger LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $$
  | BEGIN
  |   RAISE EXCEPTION 'la tabla % es inmutable (%)', TG_TABLE_NAME, TG_OP USING ERRCODE = 'integrity_constraint_violation';
  | END;
  | $$
  ' Rastro de auditoría de SOLO-AGREGAR (CLAUDE.md regla 11): payout.service.ts (INSERT … SELECT … WHERE NOT EXISTS) y reconciliation.service.ts (INSERT) son los únicos que escriben
  ' y no hay UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE sobre ella en services/*/src, test/ ni e2e/. Una política de retención o de supresión sería un procedimiento aparte (decisión de legal), no un DELETE suelto.
  TRIGGER settlement_audit_immutable : BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE ON settlement_audit FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION forbid_mutation()
  TRIGGER settlement_audit_no_truncate : BEFORE TRUNCATE ON settlement_audit FOR EACH STATEMENT EXECUTE FUNCTION forbid_mutation()
}

@enduml
